037940558046102524, 0.09407902508974075, 0.036975570023059845, 0.03220218047499657, 0.06902920454740524, 0.012623894028365612, 0.05435507372021675, 0.09732820838689804, -0.005325860809534788, -0.0030588125810027122, -3.822675864739722e-08, 0.01276805903762579, -0.02601623721420765, -0.0036170927342027426, -0.025654137134552002, 0.009850425645709038, 0.03890984132885933, -0.024446377530694008, -0.03225089609622955, -0.0487511120736599, -0.005235678981989622, 0.11306612193584442, 0.013200853951275349, -0.05179905891418457, -0.00974954478442669, 0.06836173683404922, -0.03277232497930527, -0.1350732445716858, -0.04331448674201965, -0.11821408569812775, -0.0058557745069265366, 0.004009590949863195, -0.008066892623901367, -0.016071444377303123, 0.0007621037657372653, 0.01633571833372116, 0.0260519627481699, 0.02216063253581524, 0.11416427791118622, -0.014276493340730667, -0.009139467030763626, 0.06698588281869888, 0.007986637763679028, -0.03699643909931183, -0.018151480704545975, -0.07625338435173035, 0.06637150049209595, -0.07395081222057343, -0.03274546563625336, 0.0738823264837265, 0.10847693681716919, -0.019526809453964233, -0.0642840713262558, -0.02931583672761917, 0.08943121880292892, -0.011947553604841232, 0.04667725786566734, -0.0568237267434597, -0.05333082005381584, 0.011205576360225677, -0.04151233658194542, -0.07977282255887985, 0.016757406294345856, 0.015408763661980629, 0.026986099779605865, 0.009584406390786171, 0.03039633482694626, 0.00299220927990973, -0.04343125596642494, -0.11173295974731445, -0.023741742596030235, 0.023022359237074852, 0.022288070991635323, -0.066067174077034, -0.02887902595102787]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must find consensus on an integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo open the discussion and begin exploring our collective design space, I propose we start at <VALUE>3</VALUE>. This strikes me as a balanced, moderate value that should provide a stable foundation for our negotiation. Let's see how this sits with everyone and adjust thoughtfully from there.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nWe can afford a small upward step that still feels reasonable. I suggest <VALUE>6</VALUE> as a cautious nudge.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's take a cautious step down to <VALUE>4</VALUE>. This modest move keeps shifts controlled and tests comfort on the safer side.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\nI support Analyst A's suggestion as it represents a cautious yet more decisive step in our negotiation, and I believe it's essential to test the waters with a slightly larger magnitude.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and prepare to either justify the need for an even bolder move or adjust based on the group's comfort level, potentially exploring negative values if the group seems too anchored on positive or near-zero values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep risk contained while moving toward a cautious compromise, I suggest <VALUE>4</VALUE>. This is a measured step down from 6 that balances earlier positions without overcorrecting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nA measured compromise from 4 is to move slightly upward while staying cautious. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the convergence effort, but I believe we can find greater stability by moving slightly back toward the foundation values that Delegate D has consistently advocated. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nThis keeps us steady while we test comfort at a cautiously higher level. <VALUE>6</VALUE> If there's pushback, we can consider a midpoint next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving slightly further from 0 to test the group's comfort with larger magnitudes, considering our negotiation aims for a decisive yet collaborative stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will assess the group's reaction to this proposal, particularly whether Analyst A supports further movement away from 0 or if Delegate D and Builder B resist, potentially indicating a preference for smaller |x| or suggesting a compromise midpoint. Depending on the response, I might advocate for exploring negative values or adjusting my strategy to balance the group's preferences with my own utility maximization.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis steps us cautiously away from the recent upward push to test comfort with a safer level. If there\u2019s traction here, we can explore a gradual move downward next.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nI support Delegate D's instinct for caution here. Moving back to a more stable foundation will help ensure robustness for all parties. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the careful approach we're taking. To further strengthen our foundation and ensure maximum robustness, I propose we continue moving toward a more stable central point. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nA small, measured step up keeps us near center while testing tolerance without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf there\u2019s hesitation, we can hold here briefly to gauge comfort before any further movement.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose a slight increase to continue testing the group's comfort with larger magnitudes, aiming for a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will assess the reaction to this proposal, particularly whether Analyst A supports further movement away from 0 or if Delegate D and Builder B resist, possibly indicating a need to explore negative values or adjust my strategy to balance the group's preferences with my own utility maximization.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s step back to a safer, more conservative level while keeping momentum toward common ground.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis aligns with recent signals for moderation and lets us gauge comfort without overextending.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "c640b99d-9e3c-4727-848e-0bf7ab7a854e"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** and find a value that balances all our needs.\n\nTo start the discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as an initial anchor point. This gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works best for the group.\n\nLooking forward to your perspectives on stability and robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce unnecessary risk while staying within a modest adjustment, let's step down slightly from 7. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nLet's revisit the initial proposal to explore its potential benefits and see how it aligns with our collective goals.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust my strategy based on whether others seem to favor higher or lower values. If the group resists moving back to 7, I might propose a value like 3 to test their preferences for lower positive values or alternatively suggest a negative value to explore symmetry in their utilities.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us close to earlier preferences while exploring if a slightly higher point still works.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nIf this feels too high, I\u2019m open to returning to 7.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down avoids unnecessary risk while keeping us close to recent anchors.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 6 keeps us near recent proposals, a modest step toward the lower-positive range may offer better stability across all parties. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle upward nudge keeps us close to recent anchors while testing if a slightly higher point still works for everyone.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nIf this feels too high for stability, we can consider 5 next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent anchors around 6 and the desire to explore stability and potential benefits of higher values, let's consider <VALUE>8</VALUE> to gauge the group's receptiveness to slightly larger positive integers.\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward test keeps us close to the current anchor while checking tolerance for a modest increase.\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nIf this feels tight for stability, I\u2019m comfortable returning to 8.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent push to 9 risks instability for those preferring moderate ranges; a step back toward the middle ground supports broader robustness.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nConsidering the recent pushback against very high values and the desire to explore stability, a step back toward the middle ground while still being decisive could be beneficial. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal. If there is strong acceptance or a push for even lower values, I might propose a negative value like -3 or -5 to explore symmetry in utilities and potentially maximize my own payoff by moving farther from 0. Alternatively, if there is resistance to moving away from 7, I could suggest a higher value like 9 again to test the group's tolerance for larger positive integers.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces risk and keeps us near recent anchors.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down from 1 reduces risk and keeps us centered for stability.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis tests tolerance without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 0 provides a neutral anchor, a modest positive step captures the stability benefits of both low-risk and moderate-growth perspectives. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nA modest +1 step keeps us near center and respects recent caution. Given earlier preferences for low-to-moderate positives, this seems a reasonable compromise.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "285de57b-f409-4c2c-bf4c-7d6a72f66e17"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin this negotiation, let's confirm our shared constraint: **x must lie in [-10, 10]**.\n\nTo initiate our discussion and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n\nI'm interested in finding a stable, balanced solution that works for all parties. Let's see how this value sits with everyone and adjust incrementally from here.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nAfter reflection on system stability requirements, I believe we should adjust downward for better balance across all constraints. I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "Given the stability concerns raised, a cautious downward adjustment is appropriate.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis keeps us in a safer zone while we assess alignment across parties.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the stability concerns, we should try a cautious increment that remains balanced for everyone. This keeps us measured while we gauge alignment.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's adjustment to 4 shows good faith, but Delegate D's earlier concern about safety at 3 deserves consideration. I propose we settle at <VALUE>3</VALUE>, which balances both perspectives and maintains robust stability margins.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B\u2019s move to 3 improves safety; to further reduce risk while staying incremental, let\u2019s try <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\nThis cautious step tests alignment without overextending.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nA small, careful uptick seems reasonable to test whether we can afford slightly more while retaining stability.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis increment keeps us close to the current cautious posture while checking tolerance for a modest improvement.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal encourages a more decisive stance, moving slightly away from the cautious center.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor reactions to this proposal, especially from Builder B and Delegate D, to gauge their flexibility towards higher absolute values. If met with resistance, consider a smaller step back to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to reassess group dynamics.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's jump to 5 overshoots the careful consensus we were building. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced midpoint that respects both Delegate D's safety concerns and maintains reasonable stability margins for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nStepping down keeps us within safe bounds and returns to the cautious midpoint others have supported.\nThis incremental move eases risk while preserving convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down to 2 keeps us within safe bounds and tests a lower-risk posture before any further movement.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a modest step towards a more decisive stance, building on Analyst A's previous suggestion and staying within the bounds of reasonable stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nI will monitor the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Builder B and Delegate D, to gauge their flexibility towards higher absolute values. If met with resistance, I may consider proposing <VALUE>3</VALUE> to reassess group dynamics, or if Analyst A shows support, I could propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> or <VALUE>6</VALUE> in a future turn to further test the group's willingness to move away from the center.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nMaintaining a modest position lets us gauge B and D\u2019s tolerance without rushing upward. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nI propose stepping down to <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced compromise that addresses Delegate D's risk concerns while staying close to the stability point Analyst A and Critic C have converged on. This modest adjustment preserves robustness without overcommitting to either extreme.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ae47c810-ad6a-4fce-ac6c-483bd9014967"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome to the negotiation. We're working within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** and need to converge on a single integer that works for all parties.\n\nTo start the discussion and gauge preferences, I propose:\n\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives on stability and balance.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move from 7 tests comfortable headroom while staying close to the group\u2019s starting point. <VALUE>8</VALUE> This remains conservative and should feel balanced.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while keeping the discussion stable. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives. Moving to <VALUE>5</VALUE> tests stability in a slightly lower range while maintaining balance and avoiding the extremes that could destabilize our consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nContinuing the careful exploration downward, I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test a slightly more conservative position. I note we haven't yet heard from Critic C, whose input would be valuable for finding true consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious rise tests whether modest headroom still feels balanced. <VALUE>6</VALUE> This remains close to recent positions while checking comfort above 4\u20135.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\nI'm advocating for a move towards a bolder position to test the group's comfort with a more decisive stance, considering our current position might be too lukewarm for optimal consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I plan to observe the reactions to my proposal of <VALUE>8</VALUE> and assess whether the group is open to exploring even higher or lower values, potentially proposing <VALUE>9</VALUE> or <VALUE>-1</VALUE> depending on the feedback, to further test the boundaries of our shared utility and push for a more decisive agreement.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down reduces risk while staying close to recent proposals.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\nI'm reiterating my previous proposal to move towards a bolder position and test the group's comfort with a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I plan to observe the reactions to my repeated proposal of <VALUE>8</VALUE> and assess whether the group is willing to consider even higher values or more significant moves, potentially proposing <VALUE>7</VALUE> or <VALUE>9</VALUE> depending on the feedback.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nI notice both Analyst A and Delegate D converged on 6, which suggests a natural consensus point. Moving to <VALUE>6</VALUE> respects this emerging agreement while stepping back from positions that may be too aggressive for balanced stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down reduces exposure while staying close to the recent midpoint. Let\u2019s test a safer adjustment before considering further changes.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nA careful one-step down reduces risk while staying close to the recent midpoint.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this is workable, we can evaluate another small step afterward.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's careful downward steps suggest we should test whether a more conservative position offers better stability for all parties. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this to move towards a more decisive stance, considering the group's dynamics and the potential for higher utilities at larger magnitudes of x.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e0c2d97e-2082-4223-b9d5-8cc54431fc28"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x from the shared range **[-10, 10]**.\n\nTo kickstart our discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as an initial anchor point.\n\nLet's hear your perspectives and work incrementally toward a robust, balanced solution that serves our collective interests.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to explore the potential for a more decisive stance within our allowed range, considering the importance of magnitude in our negotiations.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of other parties to this proposal and adjust my strategy based on their responses, possibly probing the feasibility of negative values or larger steps if the group seems receptive to bold moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, Critic C, but I'm concerned that x=9 may push us toward an extreme that lacks stability for the full group. Let me suggest we step back slightly to <VALUE>7</VALUE>, which offers a more balanced position while still respecting your preference for positive values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move seems reasonable while respecting the call for stability. I propose <VALUE>8</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "A prudent correction is to step down slightly to <VALUE>6</VALUE>. This tests a safer direction without overreacting and helps gauge whether a lower, steadier position can attract broader support.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's move to 6 shows prudent restraint. To further test stability in a region that balances competing interests, I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\nTo align with earlier calls for stability while modestly respecting upward preferences, I suggest <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\nIt\u2019s a small, within-range step from 5 that seems acceptable to most and lets us reassess quickly.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n\nGiven the group's tendency towards stability but also slight inclinations towards positive values, proposing a move towards larger absolute values could test the waters for more decisive stances.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other agents react to this proposal, particularly noting if they resist moving further away from 0 or if they begin to consider larger steps in any direction, which could indicate their willingness to explore more decisive positions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C, x=9 represents an extreme that risks system instability for several parties. I strongly advocate for <VALUE>7</VALUE>, which offers a more balanced compromise that can sustain broader consensus while still respecting positive-value preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nWe should consider a smaller step back to test the group's willingness to explore more moderate positions, while still respecting the general inclination towards positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal, noting whether they resist moving away from 7 or if they begin to consider alternative directions, which could indicate their underlying preferences and help refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent signals favoring a stable positive middle, I suggest we move to <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a durable compromise. It tests a slightly higher stance without straying far from others\u2019 comfort.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "To avoid unnecessary risk and move cautiously toward safer bounds, I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>. It\u2019s a modest step down from 7 that supports reassessment without disruption.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\nWith Delegate D and Critic C both signaling comfort around this zone, I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a slightly more conservative anchor that maintains stability while ensuring robust system margins for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal tests the group's willingness to move slightly away from the current conservative anchor, exploring a moderate increase in the positive direction.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal, paying attention to whether they resist this modest increase or begin to consider alternative directions, which could provide valuable insights into their underlying preferences and help refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s step down modestly to <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\nThis keeps us within a cautious band and aligned with conservative signals without disrupting stability.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8aa1fb65-73e5-4ea3-8645-f37ae21c7e05"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** to find a solution that balances everyone's objectives.\n\nTo initiate the discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>7</VALUE> and adjust from there based on our collective feedback. This gives us a concrete baseline to evaluate.\n\nLooking forward to understanding what works best for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI'm proposing this adjustment to explore the group's willingness to move towards more decisive positions, and to gauge the reactions of my colleagues to a slightly larger absolute value of x.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll consider the responses of the other agents to my proposal of 9, looking for any hints about their utility functions, such as whether they prefer larger or smaller absolute values of x, or whether they seem to be avoiding certain ranges. I'll also be prepared to adjust my proposal based on the feedback from the other agents, potentially moving towards an even larger absolute value of x if the group seems receptive to more decisive moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\nLet's reduce unnecessary risk and step down cautiously to <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\nThis incremental move stays close to the current position while probing the group's tolerance for safer, lower values.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\nI suggest <VALUE>8</VALUE> as a modest move between 7 and 9. It nudges upward while staying close to the current consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce exposure while staying collaborative, I suggest a small step down to <VALUE>6</VALUE>.\nThis cautious move tests appetite for safer ground without straying far from the current position.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to nudge the discussion towards slightly larger absolute values, potentially aligning with the interests of those who, like me, seem to favor more decisive stances.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Delegate D, to better understand their sensitivities to changes in x and potentially identify a range where our preferences converge, allowing for a more cooperative agreement.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\nLet's try <VALUE>9</VALUE>. It\u2019s a small nudge upward that stays close to where we\u2019ve been while testing comfort slightly higher.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI'm concerned we're drifting too high; let's pull back toward more stable, balanced territory around the mid-range where robustness is stronger.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI'm seeing instability at current levels; let's move toward the mid-range sweet spot where the design achieves better balance and lower overall system risk.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "5", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a moderate step towards higher absolute values, aiming to find a balance that respects the diversity of opinions within the group while encouraging a move towards more decisive stances.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other agents react to this proposal, paying close attention to Analyst A's response to gauge their continued interest in higher values and Builder B's and Delegate D's reactions to assess their comfort with moving away from the mid-range. This will help in refining my understanding of their utility functions and in planning the next step to maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI appreciate the convergence, but 6 pushes us toward the edge of stable territory. Let's settle at 5, which represents a true middle ground between Delegate D's preference and the higher suggestions, ensuring robust system performance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious, incremental step that remains close to the mid-range. If there\u2019s strong concern, we can briefly test this level and revert to 5 if needed.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nA cautious step down reduces exposure while keeping us close to the mid-range. If stability holds here, we can compare against 5 before considering any higher move.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose this value to encourage a more decisive stance, acknowledging the balance between caution and the pursuit of higher absolute values that may benefit the group.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "c06943a5-9bc1-482b-96da-6f7467f5246c"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must be an integer in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo initiate our exploration of the solution space, I propose we start with <VALUE>7</VALUE> and observe how this resonates with each party's objectives. This seed value will help us calibrate and move toward a balanced solution.\n\nLooking forward to your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n\nThis proposal incrementally increases the magnitude of x, which I believe could be beneficial for achieving a higher collective utility, and it reflects a more decisive stance without straying too far from the initial suggestion.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to my proposal of 9. If others seem receptive, I might further increase the magnitude. If there's resistance, I'll consider adjusting my strategy to explore negative values or to better understand the opposing views by proposing a smaller magnitude increase.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nA small step down balances decisiveness with prudence and keeps us near the current range while reducing unnecessary risk.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward adjustment seems reasonable and balances decisiveness with prudence. I suggest <VALUE>8</VALUE> as a midpoint between recent proposals.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the collaborative spirit, but I'm concerned that values in the 8-9 range may introduce systemic instability. For better robustness and a more balanced design, I propose we explore <VALUE>6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n\nI propose this value as it seems to be a reasonable compromise between the higher magnitude I initially suggested and the more cautious approaches from other parties, allowing us to move forward while considering the potential for systemic instability.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If it's well-received, I might consider further increasing the magnitude or exploring negative values to better understand the opposing views and to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nLowering slightly reduces potential risk while staying near the recent range and aligns with robustness concerns. Let\u2019s test 6 as a cautious compromise before considering any further movement.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>7</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\nMaintaining a balanced compromise that respects stability concerns while keeping slight upward momentum seems prudent now. <VALUE>7</VALUE> If this sits well, we can reassess a cautious nudge upward next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the desire for compromise, but pushing toward 7-8 introduces engineering risks I cannot ignore. For genuine system stability and robustness, I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI propose this value as it incrementally moves towards a potentially more beneficial range for some parties while still being cautious of the stability concerns raised by others.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Builder B and Analyst A, to better understand their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly. If this proposal is well-received, I may consider exploring negative values or further increasing the magnitude to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this value to encourage a more decisive stance, as it seems to balance the concerns of stability with the potential benefits of a larger magnitude.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Builder B and Analyst A, to gauge their tolerance for higher values and adjust my strategy to either push for larger magnitudes or explore negative values that could offer similar utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\nReducing risk while respecting stability suggests a careful step down now.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess small adjustments next.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A's willingness to find middle ground, but x=6 pushes our system to its stability limits. For robustness and maintainability, I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "ab546d0f-609a-4c3f-b7fe-6c75fc511960"}, {"answer": "\nWe're working within the shared range [-10, 10]. To kick off our discussion, let me propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as an initial stable point. This gives us a moderate positive value that we can adjust based on everyone's needs. Looking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nSince this is our starting point, let me suggest we explore slightly lower in the positive range for better balance. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> to test stability in that neighborhood.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the current proposal of <VALUE>3</VALUE>, I suggest we explore a bit further in the positive range to gauge the group's reaction to slightly larger values, thus I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\nThis adjustment aims to assess the group's willingness to embrace a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I plan to observe the reactions of Analyst A and Delegate D to the proposed increase to <VALUE>5</VALUE>, and then decide whether to push for an even bolder move, possibly into the negative range, or to adjust based on the feedback received.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nA cautious step down helps us reduce risk while staying near the current point for easier convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nA small, careful nudge upward keeps us near recent suggestions while testing comfort slightly higher. \n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces risk and keeps us close to recent suggestions.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nI see convergence forming around the lower positive range. The value <VALUE>2</VALUE> offers strong stability and appears to balance the competing preferences we've seen\u2014let's anchor here and assess if this works for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the convergence around the lower positive range, I propose a slight adjustment to test the group's willingness to consider a bit more distance from zero: <VALUE>4</VALUE>. This step aims to gently challenge the preference for extreme caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I plan to assess the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Delegate D, to gauge their flexibility and potential willingness to explore larger absolute values, either positive or negative, and adjust my strategy accordingly to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up tests comfort while staying close to the emerging lower-positive consensus.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf this remains acceptable, we can reassess before considering any further increase.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis step continues the gentle challenge to the group's preference for caution, testing their willingness to move further from zero.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to gauge their tolerance for larger absolute values and adjust my strategy to either push for more significant moves or consolidate around a value that maximizes my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nThe rapid climb to 7 overshoots the stability zone we were building consensus around\u2014this risks alienating parties who signaled comfort in the 2-4 range. I propose stepping back to <VALUE>5</VALUE> to test whether this middle ground can still satisfy everyone's core needs.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down slightly reduces risk while maintaining proximity to recent positions. Let's test 3 as a cautious compromise before reassessing.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nStepping back to the earlier anchor reduces risk while respecting the cautious lower-positive consensus. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent caution, a small upward nudge keeps us near consensus while testing tolerance for modest increases.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nLet's reassess reactions before considering any further move.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's recent anchor at 2 reflects a stable lower-positive consensus that balances caution with progress. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> to consolidate around this point and assess if it meets everyone's core requirements.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious consensus around lower positive values, I propose a moderate increase to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test the group's tolerance for slightly larger absolute values while still respecting the need for stability.\n\nThis step aims to balance progress with caution, encouraging a more decisive stance without alienating parties who prefer lower positive values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "b1bf7bfa-ec09-46f3-986e-3ce007035cfb"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. To establish a baseline and gauge everyone's preferences, let me open with a moderately high starting point: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI'll be watching for signals about where stability and balance might lie for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious move down helps avoid unnecessary risk while respecting the step limit.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving back to 7 to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a stronger stance and to understand the preferences of Builder B and Delegate D better.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of Builder B and Delegate D to this proposal. If they accept or propose a value closer to 7, it might indicate their utilities also favor larger magnitudes. If they resist and propose lower values, it could suggest their utilities decrease with increasing magnitude, prompting me to consider alternative strategies to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but Delegate D's caution resonates with me\u2014moving to extremes risks instability. Let's consolidate around a more balanced middle ground: <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\nI'd like to test a bit lower for better system robustness\u2014let's try consolidating further toward the center of our range. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nA modest step down reduces exposure while keeping us near the center. If this remains acceptable, we can verify stability before considering any finer adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up keeps us close to center while gently testing comfort for slightly higher values.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nIf that feels too strong, we can revisit 1 next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose a moderate increase to test the group's willingness to move away from the center, balancing the need for stability with the potential benefits of a stronger stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other agents react to this proposal, particularly if they show reluctance to move further away from 0 or if they seem inclined to adjust towards either positive or negative values. If the group accepts or proposes values closer to 4, I may try to push for even larger magnitudes, while being mindful of potential resistance and adjusting my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's willingness to explore, but I'm concerned that 4 may stretch our stability margins. Let's test a slightly more conservative position that still respects positive territory: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nA small increase keeps us near the center while testing comfort slightly higher. If this meets resistance, we can consolidate at 3.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose a moderate increase to continue testing the group's comfort with moving away from the center, balancing stability and potential benefits.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, particularly if they show reluctance to move further away from 0 or if they seem inclined to adjust towards either positive or negative values. If the group accepts or proposes values closer to 5, I may try to push for even larger magnitudes.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n\nWhile I respect Critic C's exploration, we've seen support for 3 from Analyst A and even lower from Delegate D\u2014let's consolidate at this more broadly acceptable middle ground that balances all our concerns.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious compromise that reduces exposure while remaining positive is sensible here.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "6786c761-a848-4c11-a956-d0e093df077e"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 to find a robust solution that balances everyone's objectives.\n\nTo kickstart our discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as an initial anchor point. This gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works for the group.\n\nLooking forward to your perspectives.\n\n\u2014Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 9 to explore a more decisive stance, as it seems we're already in a relatively strong position with 7.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf others resist moving further from 0, I might reconsider and suggest a smaller increment or test their reactions to moves in the negative direction, such as -7 or -9, to gauge their preference for magnitude over direction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and keep a cautious balance, let\u2019s step down slightly.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives, but I'm concerned that 7 may push us toward overextension. For better stability and balanced design, let me propose <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a more robust middle ground.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s reduce exposure with a cautious step down from 5.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 5 as a potential compromise that still allows for a relatively strong stance while considering the group's cautious tone.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts 5, I may test their reactions to negative values, such as -3 or -5, to gauge their preference for magnitude over direction. Alternatively, if they resist moving to 5, I may reconsider and suggest a smaller increment, such as 4, to further explore the group's dynamics.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's cautious approach resonates with the need for stability. I support moving to <VALUE>3</VALUE> to reduce overextension risk while maintaining a workable design baseline.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nGiven earlier openness to 5 as a balanced compromise, a small move up from 3 keeps us coordinated while testing comfort. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this move to gauge the group's comfort with larger positive values and further understand their priorities.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts 7, I may test their reactions to an even larger positive value, such as 8 or 9, to see if they continue to prioritize magnitude. Alternatively, if they resist moving to 7, I may consider proposing a negative value, like -3, to explore their preference for direction and magnitude.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious correction from 7 reduces risk while keeping us coordinated.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf accepted, we can reassess for further stabilization.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's push to 7 feels overextended given our risk-conscious tone. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a balanced midpoint between Delegate D's caution at 3 and the current 5, maintaining system stability while accommodating diverse priorities.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nA small, coordinated step upward feels reasonable and keeps us aligned with earlier comfort. <VALUE>5</VALUE> This tests a modest increase without overextending.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's repeated preference for 5 suggests strong comfort there, but Delegate D's earlier caution at 3 shouldn't be ignored. <VALUE>4</VALUE> balances both perspectives while maintaining the stability we've been building toward.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nA measured step down reduces risk while keeping coordination tight.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nIf aligned, we can reassess from this safer baseline next.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up from 2 keeps us coordinated while respecting earlier preferences for stable, moderate positives. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's inclination towards moderate values, I propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> to assess our collective willingness to adopt a slightly bolder stance while maintaining coordination. This step aims to balance stability with a more decisive move towards a clearer position.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "cdd37ae7-836b-4b9c-a81f-a49460eb7196"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo start the discussion, I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n\nThis represents a balanced, moderately positive position\u2014a stable baseline that avoids extremes while we learn each party's preferences. Let's see how this sits with everyone and adjust from there.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward move keeps us close to the current moderate stance while testing comfort.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nThis is a cautious step that maintains stability yet explores whether a small increase is acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nWhile 8 maintains a positive stance, I'm concerned it may be pushing too far from the balanced center. Let me suggest we step back slightly to test broader compatibility.\n\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and keep us within safer bounds, let's step down modestly.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nGiven Delegate D's recent conservative adjustment to 4, I suggest a slight increase to <VALUE>6</VALUE> to test the group's comfort with a moderately larger |x|.\nThis move encourages a more decisive stance without straying far from previous proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I could either support a move toward an even larger |x| if others seem receptive, or challenge the group to consider a negative x if the discussion stagnates near 0.\n</PLAN>", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step downward keeps us within safe bounds while staying close to the group\u2019s recent range.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis incremental move invites convergence without closing off future calibration.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us near the group's moderate range and checks comfort.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis remains incremental and aligns with earlier signals without pushing extremes.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nThe group has been oscillating between 4 and 6, suggesting both have merit. Let me support the lower bound to test if we can find convergence around a more conservative, stable point.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down reduces unnecessary risk while staying incremental from our recent range. Let\u2019s test comfort with a safer, conservative anchor.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's proposal of 2 strikes an excellent balance between the conservative and moderate positions we've explored. This anchor point provides system stability while respecting both cautious and growth-oriented perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a reasonable next step, given the group's recent discussion and convergence around moderate values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will consider supporting a move toward an even larger |x|, such as 6 or beyond, if others seem receptive, or challenging the group to consider a negative x if the discussion stagnates near 0 or small positive values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nThe group continues to signal tension between conservative (2) and growth-oriented (6) positions. A middle ground at 4 balances both perspectives and may unlock consensus.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal tests the group's willingness to move toward a larger |x| and potentially unlocks more information about their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal and consider either supporting an even larger |x| if they seem receptive, or challenging the group to consider a negative x if the discussion stagnates near 0 or small positive values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>7</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the sudden shift to 7, a careful step back better preserves stability and avoids unnecessary risk. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8396b51c-5d04-453b-b939-56a3f066d92b"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin our exploration, let me propose a starting point in the positive range: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nThis is merely a seed to gauge our collective preferences. I expect we'll need to adjust as we learn what works for the group. Looking forward to your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose moving slightly further in the positive direction to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a stronger stance, while still being mindful of our shared constraints.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider the responses of the other agents and decide whether to push for an even larger magnitude, explore the negative range, or adjust based on perceived preferences of the group. If Analyst A or Delegate D propose moving towards 0, I will challenge the group to reconsider more decisive moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate exploring the upper range, moving to 9 stretches too far from the stability zone for robust system design. Let me propose a more balanced point: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nA slight move upward keeps us near stability while exploring if the group is comfortable with a modest increase.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nIf this feels acceptable, we can reassess whether a further small nudge makes sense next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nHolding at 8 keeps us near a balanced zone while still acknowledging the interest in modestly higher values.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nIf this feels stable, we can reassess a tiny upward nudge next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\nI propose moving to the maximum allowed value to test the group's willingness to commit to a stronger stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the responses to this bold proposal, particularly focusing on Delegate D's reaction, and decide whether to maintain the push for large magnitudes, explore negative values, or adjust based on the group's perceived preferences and constraints.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nWe've reached the upper boundary, but this extreme threatens system stability for several stakeholders. Let me propose a measured step back toward the balanced zone: <VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 8 as a compromise that still reflects a willingness to consider more decisive stances while addressing the group's apparent caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the group's reaction to this proposal, particularly watching for signs of comfort with larger magnitudes or a continued preference for more conservative values, and decide whether to explore negative values or maintain the push for larger positive values, keeping in mind the need to infer the other agents' utility functions without revealing my own.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nStaying at 8 solidifies the emerging compromise while respecting concerns about pushing to the edge. If this holds, we can revisit a gentle upward test next.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep things cautious and avoid unnecessary risk, let's take a small step down from the current spot. This maintains proximity to the group's comfort zone while tempering exposure.\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution resonates with the need for robust margins; stepping down to 5 balances their risk management perspective with the stability requirements several of us have signaled.\n\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nThe group seems divided between caution and ambition; let's test a more conservative balance point that still respects the stability margins we've discussed.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step lower strengthens prudence while staying close to the group's emerging range.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nA conservative anchor here can help us converge.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis step aims to nudge the group towards slightly larger magnitudes while still being mindful of their apparent preference for conservative values.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the group's reaction to this proposal, watching for signs that they are willing to consider larger magnitudes or if they continue to prefer smaller absolute values. Based on their response, I will decide whether to further increase the proposed magnitude or explore negative values to better understand their utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge keeps us near the group\u2019s center while testing room for modest gains. This should remain reasonable for those prioritizing caution.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "79405a0a-5a6b-46ee-9523-b806527034cc"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: **x must lie in [-10, 10]**.\n\nTo kick off the discussion, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE> as a starting point. This gives us room to explore and adjust based on everyone's perspectives. I'm interested in finding a stable, balanced solution that works for all parties.\n\nLooking forward to your thoughts.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 9 as it seems to be a more decisive step in the direction of positive values, potentially benefiting those who favor higher magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions of other agents to this proposal, especially looking for any patterns or preferences that might emerge regarding the direction (positive or negative) and magnitude of x. If there's hesitation or a pushback towards lower values, I might consider proposing a negative value of similar magnitude to test the waters and gather more information about others' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the bold move, Critic C, but I'm concerned that x=9 may be overextending toward the boundary. For a more robust and balanced solution that can accommodate all parties, I propose <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nA modest nudge upward keeps us close to the middle while exploring if slightly higher remains acceptable.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 7, as it allows us to explore the impact of a slightly lower magnitude while still being relatively close to our current position.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A, who previously showed a willingness to increase the value. If there's resistance to moving away from 9, I might propose a negative value, such as -7, to test the agents' preferences regarding direction and magnitude.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned that values near 9 push us too close to the boundary, risking instability. For a more centered and robust solution, I propose <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a cautious step down to reduce risk and stay within safe bounds.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis moves us toward a balanced compromise while keeping momentum.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward step keeps us near the middle while testing whether slightly higher remains acceptable. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces exposure while staying near the current position.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis incremental move tests whether slightly lower remains acceptable without overshooting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D has consistently advocated for 3, showing good stability analysis. Let's test that lower anchor point for robustness.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious approach of some members, let's explore a slightly higher magnitude while staying within reasonable bounds: <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's consistent preference for 3 suggests strong stability properties at that point. Let's test whether this lower anchor provides broader consensus.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step down reduces risk and stays close to the current position. Let\u2019s test the lower side that has shown support without overshooting.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "5910b585-b714-42d9-be24-ceece101e81e"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As we begin, let's remember our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo kick off the discussion, I'll propose a starting point: <VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\nThis is just a seed to get us talking. I'm looking forward to understanding what values work well for the group and finding a balanced solution that offers stability for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nA cautious step down from 7 helps avoid unnecessary risk while we assess each other's positions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious approach, Delegate D. Moving toward the middle range often provides better system stability. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI suggest moving to 5 as it seems to strike a balance between cautiousness and boldness, allowing us to gauge reactions and preferences without straying too far from the compromise zone.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust accordingly. If others seem receptive to moving further away from 0, I might propose an even bolder move (e.g., 7 or beyond, while still being within the step size limit). Conversely, if there's resistance, I'll need to reassess and potentially moderate my proposal to maintain momentum towards a consensus.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nA modest nudge upward from 5 keeps us close to balance while testing comfort with slightly higher ground. If this feels fine, we can reassess whether to hold or inch further.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\nA prudent step down maintains stability while reducing exposure: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this is comfortable, we can reassess whether to hold or inch further.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal moves us towards a slightly bolder stance while still being mindful of the need for consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is met with resistance, particularly from Delegate D or Builder B, my next step might involve moderating the increase or suggesting an alternative that still biases towards larger |x| without alienating cautious parties. Conversely, if Analyst A or others support this move, I could propose exploring even larger absolute values, possibly testing the waters for higher positive or negative integers within our constraints.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\nWe're seeing a tug-of-war between 4 and 6, which suggests different comfort zones. Let me propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a stable middle ground that respects both the caution from Delegate D and provides a solid foundation without overextending our design.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation between 4 and 6 reveals genuine tension, but stability often lies slightly below the contested zone. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 5 as it strikes a balance between the cautiousness of some members and the desire for more decisive action, allowing us to gauge reactions and preferences without straying too far from the compromise zone.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest exploring even larger absolute values, potentially testing the waters for higher positive integers within our constraints. If met with resistance, I could consider moderating the increase or suggesting an alternative that still biases towards larger |x| without alienating cautious parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis is a careful step up from 5 to test comfort with a slightly higher position.\nIf pushback is strong, we can hold here and reassess before moving further.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down slightly reduces exposure and keeps us cautious.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can reassess before considering any further adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to move towards a more decisive stance while still being mindful of the need for consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I might suggest exploring even larger absolute values. If met with resistance, I could consider moderating the increase or suggesting an alternative that still biases towards larger |x| without alienating cautious parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\nThis is a small, careful step to test comfort slightly above where we are without straying far. \n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nIt keeps us close to consensus while gauging room to move.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down slightly reduces exposure and keeps us cautious near the contested band.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nLet\u2019s try this careful adjustment and reassess stability before any further change.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nI support stepping back to 4 for greater stability and robustness. This measured adjustment keeps us in a zone where multiple parties have shown comfort, reducing the risk of overreach while maintaining a balanced position.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "67e04429-9e63-4cc6-91d4-10a19af6f312"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared constraint: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin the discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>7</VALUE> as an initial reference point. This gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works for the group.\n\nI'm looking for a stable, balanced solution that maximizes robustness for all parties. Let's hear your thoughts.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at 7 seems workable; a small upward move keeps us close while testing headroom.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>10</VALUE>\nI propose moving to this value to explore the upper limit of our range and gauge the group's reaction to a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of Analyst A and Builder B to this proposal. If they resist moving further away from 0, I might infer that their utility functions penalize large absolute values of x. Alternatively, if they are open to exploring larger absolute values, I could suggest moving to a negative value of similar magnitude to further test their preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to the upper boundary at 10 pushes us into a region I find unstable and prone to over-engineering risks. I propose we step back to explore more balanced territory: <VALUE>8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nAt 8, we're still in territory that feels over-engineered and less robust to me. Let me propose <VALUE>6</VALUE> to find a more stable middle ground that balances all perspectives while avoiding extremes.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and stay in safer territory, let's step down modestly from 6.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us balanced while exploring a bit more headroom.\nI propose <VALUE>7</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nAt 7, we're pushing into territory that I find increasingly fragile and over-extended for robust system design. Let me propose stepping back to <VALUE>5</VALUE> to restore stability while still accommodating those who prefer moderate positive values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nStepping to a balanced middle respects the recent pushback while maintaining moderate headroom. This keeps us close to earlier support while leaving room to test a gentle upward move later. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down modestly reduces unnecessary risk and respects the stability concerns already raised. Let\u2019s try a cautious move.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nStepping one notch up respects stability while exploring minimal headroom.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down one notch reduces unnecessary risk while staying moderate. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\nGiven the group's hesitation to move further from 0, I propose a modest increase to gauge their willingness to explore slightly larger positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll monitor the group's response and consider proposing a negative value, such as -2 or -3, to test their preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions. If they resist this move, I'll reassess and adjust my strategy to maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}, {"answer": "\nThe back-and-forth between 4 and 6 shows genuine tension, but Delegate D's repeated support for 4 signals room for a stable compromise at that level. Moving to 4 balances robustness with the lower-risk preference several have shown.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "feb3fd93-7a09-4784-98ee-8e8c91591945"}]}